Fix search dropdown width, unreadable title text, and broken result clicks

Widen the search dropdown past the sidebar (Option A from discussion):
it was pinned at left:0;right:0 inside the 186px sidebar, so every
result row got squeezed into ~166px and wrapped illegibly with a
stray horizontal scrollbar. Now it's a fixed 380px flyout (capped at
viewport width minus margin on narrow windows) that floats out over
the main content instead of being boxed in by its parent.

Fix unreadable result titles: .lib-title has no explicit color and
relies on inheriting one from its ancestors - fine on the Library
page where .lib-card sets color:var(--bone), but .search-dropdown
never set a color of its own, so it fell through to the page's
default (light-background) text color rendered on the dropdown's
dark panel background. Added color:var(--bone) directly to
.search-dropdown so everything inside it (title, hit buttons)
inherits the right color for a dark background.

Fix two navigation bugs in the five search destination handlers
(searchProps in App()):
- None of them closed Account/Settings before navigating. Those are
  checked ahead of `section` in the render switch, so clicking a
  result while either panel was open just looked like nothing
  happened. All five now call setAccountOpen(false)/setSettingsOpen(false)
  first.
- onOpenItem only set `open` and `section`, never touched `nav`. But
  Detail renders with items={mine}, which is filtered by
  nav.speciesId - so a stale or null nav.speciesId (e.g. landing from
  the species grid) meant Detail got an items list that didn't
  contain the item it was told to open, which crashed the render and
  produced the blank white screen Matt hit. onOpenItem now looks up
  the item's species via its genetics line and calls go() to point
  nav at the right tree before setting `open`.

Build and lint clean - same pre-existing 3 unused-var errors and 1
exhaustive-deps warning, nothing new.

